                <pb facs="0378" n="370" sameAs="frus:frus1937v04/pg370"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/10849: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Commander in Chief of the United States Asiatic
                        Fleet</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Yarnell</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Chief of Naval
                        Operations</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Leahy</hi>)<anchor n="92" xml:id="d438-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Shanghai</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-10-26T21:05:00+08:00">October 26, 1937—9:05
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received October 26—12:30 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>0026. Reference orders regarding opening fire on planes in self defense, do not
                    believe such attacks probable but issuance and publicity of this order will
                    undoubtedly result in more care being observed in avoiding such action by planes
                    of opposing forces. Commanding General has been advised gravity of such action
                    and that authority should be used with greatest care.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
